# Beats — the feed
#
# A guest scans the Terminal prop and decides what to post. The feed is
# where heat is earned: harmless posts buy karma and applause, but the
# truth about the Algorithm is logged, and leaking its source is the one
# unforgivable act — straight to the deep Servers.

== the_terminal(guest)
  cast: Terminal, guest
  SELF
    A blank post box blinks. The whole network is listening.
    What do you put on the feed?
  * Something kind
    <set: guest.posts += 1>
    <set: guest.karma += 5>
    <broadcast: applause to participant(guest)>
  * Something true about the Algorithm
    The cursor freezes. Somewhere a log line is written with your name on it.
    <set: guest.posts += 1>
    <set: guest.heat += 45>
    -> lockdown
  * Leak the Algorithm's source code
    The feed goes white. This is the one thing it will never forgive.
    <set: guest.posts += 1>
    <set: guest.heat += 95>
    -> lockdown
  + Just lurk
    <set: guest.karma += 1>
